5,What Languages do People Speak in Nigeria?,https://worldpopulationreview.com/countries/nigeria/language,"It is from the Niger-Congo language family and has as many as 24 million native speakers, both within and outside of Nigeria. There are over 20 dialects of Igbo, but Umuahia and Owerri are considered to be the official dialects.Samba Daka. 107,000. Koro Wachi.",Samba Daka,Niger-Congo
6,Daka language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/daka_language,"The Daka language, also known as Chamba Daka or Samba Daka (ISO 639-3: ccg), is an indigenous language of the Dakoid branch of the Northern Bantoid languages within the Niger-Congo family, spoken prim.",Samba Daka,Niger-Congo
